{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And you shall place of your splendor upon him.</b> You shall apportion him honor before all Israel. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: 'Of your splendor' — and not all your splendor. The face of Moses was like the face of the sun; the face of Joshua was like the face of the moon. And this wondrous parable comes to indicate the level of prophecy of each one: for the level of Moses' prophecy was through the Special Name, which is the force of the sun, and the level of Joshua's prophecy was through 'splendor' (הוד), which is the force of the moon. Now this is the parable; but the meaning of the parable is: just as the light of the moon is not from itself but only from the sun — for the moon receives its light from it — so too Joshua received from Moses. And just as the sun receives its light from elsewhere — and concerning this Scripture said (Genesis 1:14): ״יהי מאורות״, and it did not say ״יהי אורים״ but rather ״מאורות״, that is to say, receivers of light — so too Moses our master, peace be upon him, received from the Special Name."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:37.177384900Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}